course: dictionary
lesson: 8369
title: Roundness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Roundness is a noun. It means the quality of being round or curved, like a circle or a ball. A circle is perfectly round, so it has a lot of roundness. You can see roundness in a football, a coin or a bowl.
explain: The word can also describe a full, smooth quality, such as a rich sound or a smooth, full taste. The meaning is different, but the feeling is similar: nothing sharp or flat. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Artists use roundness to make pictures look real. They show roundness by shading «the side away from the light». Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Roundness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say the roundness, not a roundness.
fact: «Roundness» means the quality of being round or curved, like a circle or a ball.
fact: The roundness of the Earth means it is close to a sphere, like a giant ball.
fact: Because the Earth is round, ships seem to disappear over the horizon.
fact: «Roundness» can also mean a full, smooth quality, as in the roundness of a sound or taste.
exercise: What does roundness mean? | Being very tall and thin | A sharp point at the end | A loud, harsh noise | *The quality of being round or curved, like a circle or ball
exercise: Artists show roundness by shading the side away from the light. What does this shading help a drawing look like? | A noisy picture | A flat, bright picture | A shrinking picture | *A solid, 3D object
exercise: Scientists say the roundness of the Earth explains why ships seem to disappear over the horizon. What does this mean? | It is square with straight edges | It is perfectly flat, like a table | *It is close to a sphere, like a giant ball | It is hollow inside, like a tube
test: What does the roundness of her voice mean, if it is a full, smooth sound? | *A full, smooth quality | A thin, sharp quality | A quiet, shaky quality
test: Which word is the noun meaning the quality of being round? | rounded | roundly | round | *roundness
exam: Ella says roundness means a square shape. What is the correct meaning? | *Being round or curved, like a circle or ball | Being square with four straight sides | Being very long and thin | Being loud and fast
